bcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/701860-mermaids?p=702497#post702497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gangrel Mariners are already a canon part of the game. They're a weird quasi-bloodline that seems to occur in Gangrel that choose aquatic lifestyles. Unlike a full bloodline, childer of Mariners aren't forced to be Mariners themselves. They can chose to live on land an stay normal Gangrel instead.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even among the mariners &quot;legs into fish tail&quot; is probably a rather rare feature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T08:31:21-07:00","id":703497,"title":"","content":"Mermaids and similar mythological creatures have had varied descriptions and attributes over time.<br /> <br /> For example, many mermaids were depicted as still having two legs, each leg having scales and a fin at the end of it, rather than one combined leg (which explained how men were supposed to be seduced into having sex with one).<br /> <br /> If you're just focusing on the modern conceptualization of mermaids, yes, the Mariners aren't a great fit (though you did discuss &quot;not traditional choices&quot; with the Gangrel). But if we're including a wider array of mythology and depictions through the ages, this isn't really a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}]