 </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You may be forgetting all the bits where they go around hammering people to death with their gigantic scrotums. That's actually a mythological thing. Also proof that the Japanese have strange fixations with genitals <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you mean humans in general? Else why would so many people envision their parts falling off because someone else is in charge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T17:40:55-07:00","id":707773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/701860-mermaids?p=706427#post706427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Came across an apparently independent reference to tanuki as badgers - don't know where they found it, but they don't refer to anything else from 8MD. However, even there, raccoon dogs were the primary tanuki basis, and there was no mention of them as fighters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Read their writeup in land of 8 million dreams they are combatants, they turn into badgers its very much at odds with anything I've seen of them in Japanese culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T01:00:48-07:00","id":708360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/701860-mermaids?p=707773#post707773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Read their writeup in land of 8 million dreams they are combatants, they turn into badgers its very much at odds with anything I've seen of them in Japanese culture.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wikipedia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;<i>Tanuki</i>&quot; is often mistakenly translated into English as &quot;badger&quot; or &quot;raccoon&quot; (as used in the US version of the movie <i>Pom Poko</i>, and outlined in Tom Robbins' book <i>Villa Incognito</i>)</div> </div> </div> </div>I've actually thought that Tanuki were racoons for the better part of the late 90s, thanks to shoddy American translations. Do consider that when the book was written, internet wasn't as ubiquitous and they went with the sources they had. Also, the Racoon and Tanuki thing are quite a bit of a mess, since it seems that this was actually a longer standing <a href=\"http://www.onmarkproductions.com/html/tanuki.shtml\" target=\"_blank\">cultural problem with translation</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/701860-mermaids?p=706831#post706831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't you mean humans in general? Else why would so many people envision their parts falling off because someone else is in charge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Touche.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T06:46:04-07:00","id":708690,"title":"","content":"Other shortcomings of Lo8MD:<br /> <br /> - Someone thought that Chu-ih-yu was passible Mandarin. It almost is... if you take out the u between the Ch and ih. This leads me to believe that the metal kamuii are actually supposed to be the Ch'ih-yu (Hanyu Pinyin Chi You), which fits the naming pattern for the Chinese names coming from the Legendary Emperors era along with the Hou-chi (HP Houji) and the Suijen (HP Sui Ren)<br /> - Text box on Chinese languages low-balls various sounds as having &quot;six different meanings&quot;, which seems like it might be a misunderstanding of the minimum number of tones people count as being a part of Cantonese.<br /> - Some other kith names are off for the basic pronunciation guides; the hsi in Fu Hsi is pronounced syee or like the Sidhe if you you're in a real hurry to explain it, not hisee, and for the Heng.Po, po is actually pronounced more like paw.<br /> - Note for the hanumen: gibbons are not monkeys, either by folk taxonomy or by primatologist standards. They don't have tails, part of the reason why.<br /> - Hsien xian. Ha ha ha ha ha!... the way it's formed, it doesn't mean what it says it does. It actually means &quot;Every Daoist Superbeing&quot;, because that's what repeating the same character does (\u4eba\u4eba, renren means &quot;everybody&quot;, for example).<br /> - The alchemies for wood and metal use forest and iron instead of the typical characters one would expect.<br /> - The title &quot;xuicai&quot; should be xiucai. Xui is not a sound used in pinyin-rendered Mandarin. Typos with Romanization can be brutal.<br /> - For Yu titles, count seems to have been made to use the character that would also be used by the five-dot title of mandarin. It's differentiated in alphabetic type solely with a different Romanization.<br /> - The freebie point cost chart for the two different hsien types is flipped and doesn't have the cost listed for Tao.<br /> - In case you were wondering, you pronounce I Chih as something like &quot;ee juh&quot;.<br /> - Another thing that needed authorial clarification, the yugen gained from being around festivals is apparently left unlisted.<br /> - Given the way that most of Waigoren is Romanized, it should be waiguoren. (Most of it is in Hanyu Pinyin, but the go is used in Wade-Giles for the pinyin guo)<br /> - i'm still going to complain about Chi'n Ta even though it's not a thing about Lo8MD specifically. Ch'in-ta, people. Ch'in-ta. Assuming you even want to use the term &quot;clan of strikes&quot; for mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T13:07:14-07:00","id":709191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/701860-mermaids?p=708360#post708360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I've actually thought that Tanuki were racoons for the better part of the late 90s, thanks to shoddy American translations. Do consider that when the book was written, internet wasn't as ubiquitous and they went with the sources they had. Also, the Racoon and Tanuki thing are quite a bit of a mess, since it seems that this was actually a longer standing <a href=\"http://www.onmarkproductions.com/html/tanuki.shtml\" target=\"_blank\">cultural problem with translation</a><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I think if they had went with the Racoon translation it would have been more in keeping with the myths. The Tanuki 8mdreams get saddled with all sorts of western associations with badgers, gruff survivors, scary combatants etc. That wouldn't have shown up except for badgerism. Racoons having a more trickster view in the west would probably have ended up matching things better.<br /> <br /> I'd have made the Hanumen the token combatants, even it it was a more tricksy combat style. I mean their two blatant sources of inspiration are serious on the punching skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T13:09:20-07:00","id":709193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/701860-mermaids?p=709191#post709191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly I think if they had went with the Racoon translation it would have been more in keeping with the myths. The Tanuki 8mdreams get saddled with all sorts of western associations with badgers, gruff survivors, scary combatants etc. That wouldn't have shown up except for badgerism. Racoons having a more trickster view in the west would probably have ended up matching things better.<br /> <br /> I'd have made the Hanumen the token combatants, even it it was a more tricksy combat style. I mean their two blatant sources of inspiration are serious on the punching skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, they get two more dots of Dexterity. That's actually a pretty notable advantage, above and beyond being really good at offensive Metal alchemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T17:27:33-07:00","id":709584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/701860-mermaids?p=709193#post709193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, they get two more dots of Dexterity. That's actually a pretty notable advantage, above and beyond being really good at offensive Metal alchemy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah but for some reason Str/Sta are considered more combaty even if mechanically its not as sound..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T07:49:51-07:00","id":710535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/701860-mermaids?p=709584#post709584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah but for some reason Str/Sta are considered more combaty even if mechanically its not as sound..</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the classic WoD does use Exalted Power Combat/2e clinch rules, where it counts for targeting and damage. Those high-Rage Gurahl Hugbears are deadly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T14:33:06-07:00","id":711247,"title":"","content":"I remember my jaw dropping when I found out tanuki were a real animal and not just a mythological variant on raccoons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}